Your instincts have been altered, diverging from human norms and being recontextualized around your powers. The ways this can manifest are myriad; 

For example, if you could consume magic or some other kind of energy, you would feel an instinctive drive to consume it, while a regenerative power might reduce your instinctive avoidance of physical harm, even removing it outright if the regeneration is strong enough. 

This is most noticeable with species altering powers such as Lucky Mutations or Ascensions, majorly replacing human instincts with those of your new species.

You acquire a Bio-Boosted Armor, also known as Guyver, a mysterious symbiotic bio-organic environmental suit that bonds with its host at a genetic level. This extraordinary armor enhances the host's innate capabilities and provides an array of advanced bio-organic systems, including organ removal and rearrangement, DNA splicing, and elimination of the need for regular sleep or food consumption, all while shielding the host from external interferences such as telepathic control (psionic shielding).

Despite its resilience, an activated Guyver can still sustain damage or even be destroyed with the appropriate tools, such as specially designed corrosive chemical compounds capable of dissolving the armor, any biological plague made or effect from a Bio-manipulation power, or raw power of sufficient magnitude. The Guyver Unit itself exhibits semi-sentience and can operate independently to a limited extent if its host is unable to control it consciously. In such cases, it primarily acts to preserve the host from perceived threats. This semi-sentience also prevents the host from disengaging the armor in situations where its protection and healing abilities are crucial for survival.

One of the most remarkable features of the Guyver is its regenerative abilities. It can rapidly regrow significant portions of the host's brain and skull within seconds, and even regenerate fully from just a few attached cells on the control medal. Even when only a fraction of the host remains, it can regenerate into a complete organism in a matter of minutes.

On the weapons side, the Guyver armor boasts an impressive arsenal:

Vibration Globes: Capable of homing in on molecular resonance frequencies, causing objects to disintegrate into particles;
Thoratic Particle Beam Cannon: A high-energy particle beam weapon delivering over 100 Megawatts of power, though it requires significant energy and cannot be fired repeatedly;
Head Beam: A multi-directional infrared laser utilizing body heat, concentrated and expelled through a laser generator;
High-Frequency Swords: Blades reinforced by alternating current, vibrating at high frequencies to weaken molecular bonds and enhance cutting ability;
Gravity Controller: Harnesses gravitational energy from another dimension, enabling flight and unleashing destructive gravity waves;
Head Sensor: Provides electromagnetic, thermal, and vibration sensing capabilities;

The Guyver leaves growths on the host's back, acting as transceivers to the armor and sensing nearby Guyver hosts. When summoned, a signal activates the armor, and when not in use, it is stored in a sub-dimension. Your Control Medal is absorbed into you and the armor, rendering it impervious to disruption, destruction, or manipulation unless both you and the armor are completely destroyed.

You have gained absolute command over the entire Officio Assassinorum, inheriting every major Temple in its totality:

The Callidus Temple, whose operatives are unrivaled masters of disguise, infiltration, and polymorphine-driven shapeshifting;

The Culexus Temple, formed from Pariahs and Blanks whose null aura erases psychic, dimensional, and mind-based abilities, inflicting visceral torment upon all nearby—all except you;

The Eversor Temple, a legion of hyper-aggressive, chemically and genetically optimized berserkers engineered to function as unstoppable living weapons, they remain cryofrozen until they are needed;

The Vindicare Temple, peerless long-range executioners whose precision is so absolute they can eliminate even daemon-possessed targets with a single, perfectly placed shot;

The Venenum Temple, master toxicologists who craft subtle, untraceable poisons capable of killing without leaving the faintest metabolic signature;

And the Vanus Temple, clandestine saboteurs and information phantoms who manipulate politics, systems, and infrastructure from the shadows with silent, near-omniscient efficiency.

Every assassin—regardless of Temple, specialization, or augmentation—now holds for you the same depth of devotion and reverence that the average Adepta Sororitas offers the Emperor. Each possesses the full knowledge, resources, and authority required to recruit, indoctrinate, and train new operatives for their respective disciplines.

This acquisition also grants you a unique bio-implant embedded in both yourself and all members of the Temples—along with the means to create more—which provides controlled access to a dedicated pocket dimension. Within this dimension lies the entirety of the Officio Assassinorum’s facilities: their training grounds, armories, research complexes, logistical and financial infrastructure, secure operations hubs, and, at its center, a suite of fully furnished personal chambers reserved exclusively for you, this dimension can merge with any other pocket dimensions granted, such as Shadow Garden (The Eminence In the Shadow).

Created by an advanced civilization to stop beings from Beyond the Veil/Stars, the original Reality Stabilizer required construction around a star to harness its power and protected an entire solar system. However, your version is a simplified and less potent model, capable of protecting only a single planet but only requires a fraction of the energy and can function for several centuries before its internal generators need refueling.

The Dimensional Cage takes the form of a sleek, black icosahedron measuring 1 x 1 x 1 meters. Despite its compact size, it contains highly advanced machinery within a space that is larger on the inside. Once powered, the anchor projects a barrier around the planet, invisible to most except those able to perceive metaphysical or higher-dimensional phenomena. The barrier’s primary function is to tether the planet’s metaphysical space to a set of predefined rules, stabilizing reality and preventing harmful external forces from entering or altering it.

While the barrier allows most natural events and entities to pass through freely, it blocks anything classified as “harmful” by the system’s parameters. These threats include: Interdimensional beings; Reality-warping phenomena (e.g., spatial tears, time distortions, Quantum Stuff,); Certain types of metaphysical or esoteric energy; Any forces or entities that have been manually added to the Blacklist by the user;

The Blacklist feature lets you define what the barrier considers harmful. You can customize the parameters to allow specific entities or energies to bypass the defense. For example, allied magic-based attacks could be permitted while hostile reality-warpers or dimensional invaders are completely blocked.

Despite the Dimensional Cage robust metaphysical tethering mechanism, extreme or sudden surges in universal phenomena can cause temporary glitches. These disruptions may result in portions of the barrier weakening or malfunctioning, creating gaps through which certain phenomena could slip before the system stabilizes again. While these glitches are usually self-correcting, they can cause brief periods of vulnerability. Notable phenomena that can cause such disruptions include: The spontaneous and sudden existence of a new supernatural energy source near or inside the barrier; A Big Rip (a hypothetical cosmological event); Collision with another universe; The corpse of a GOD falling through your comparatively fragile 4D reality;

Note: To work, the Cage needs to be on the same reality as the planet, thus put in any type of space, time, dimension not in the same place as the planet, will instead protect it and not the planet.

A Relic organic ship control orbs has fused with your Control Medal, evolving into an upgrade module for the Guyver unit called Gigantic, the power of this module is estimated to be at least twenty times superior to the original Guyver, growing even more powerful by consuming more control orbs and a will to be strong.

Powers improvement include:

Energy Amps: Bestow the Gigantic with the ability to generate an omni-directional force field akin to a Zoalord's Barrier. They also enable control of surrounding body parts, even if severed from the main body;
Enhanced High-Frequency Wave-Vibration Swords: These swords are now flexible, capable of extending and curving to remarkable distances while being able to manifest in any part of the armor;
Tri Head Beam Orbs: The central orb boasts fifteen times the intensity of a normal Guyver's Head Beam, while the two smaller orbs match the output of a standard Guyver Head Beam;
Vibration Globes: Additional vibration globes are situated at the Gigantic's mouth, concealed by opening plates;

Giga-Beam Cannon: A devastating weapon, one hundred times more potent than the Thoratic Particle Beam Cannon, thanks to the inclusion of two extra Gravity Control Orbs embedded in each chest plate;
Gravity Knuckle: Infuses the Gigantic's fist with high-powered energy, used alongside back thrusters for a potent discharge upon impact;
Gravity Ram: By extending the chest spike and channeling energy into it, activating the Barrier shield and powering up all three gravity orbs, the Gigantic accelerates using back thrusters, obliterating the surrounding area;
Plasma Jets: Large packs beneath the shoulder blades propel the Gigantic forward at incredible speeds, surpassing its previous flight capabilities;

Additionally, the special move, Gigantic Exceed, increases the Gigantic's size to 52 meters. The orbs and chest spike glow, and the body shifts to dark colors. The three gravity orbs and power amps operate at full capacity, drawing energy from another dimension to maintain the Gigantic's enlarged form. All of the Gigantic's weapons and abilities are amplified in this form, proportional to its increased size.
